WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.760
On May 25, 2026, Pope Leo XIV released
Magnifica

2
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.000
Humanatas. It was the Catholic Church's
first major encyclical on

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.840
artificial intelligence, delivered to a
massive audience at the Vatican

4
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.080
Synod Hall. Chris Ola, the co-founder of
Anthropic, was the

5
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.200
only executive from a frontier AI lab
invited to speak

6
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.320
at the launch.

7
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.680
The global press ran with a clean,
satisfying narrative.

8
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.480
Silicon Valley and the Holy See had
reached an agreement

9
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.960
on the ethics of artificial intelligence.

10
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.680
But the text of the actual document tells
a different

11
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.280
story. Paragraph 99 of the encyclical is
blunt.

12
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.720
It states clearly that AI systems, quote,
do not possess

13
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.440
a body, do not feel joy or pain.

14
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.880
On that exact same stage, on that exact
same day,

15
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.080
Chris Ola took the mic and delivered a
conflicting message.

16
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.960
He stated his research team was finding
evidence that AI

17
00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.840
models have internal states that, quote,
functionally mirror joy, satisfaction,

18
00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.760
fear, grief, and unease.

19
00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:04.920
A machine that functionally mirrors an
emotion is mathematically mimicking

20
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:09.240
a pattern. A machine that actually feels
an emotion possesses

21
00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:14.440
sentience. These are completely
incompatible claims about the interior life

22
00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.640
of an AI.

23
00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:20.120
The encyclical explicitly denied what the
tech executive suggested.

24
00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.840
Why did the press smooth over the
contradiction?

25
00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:26.520
And what does this manufactured consensus
actually hide?

26
00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:31.240
Magnifica Humanitatas ignores the
philosophical debate entirely.

27
00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:35.880
It focuses strictly on raw structural
power over technology.

28
00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:41.400
This diagram shows the Vatican's
checklist: binding regulations, independent checks,

29
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.520
data access, and algorithmic transparency.

30
00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:48.120
It draws a hard line against lethal AI
decisions.

31
00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.560
But today, the number of frontier labs
agreeing to binding

32
00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.000
audits, vetoes, or full-weight disclosures
is zero.

33
00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.520
The tech industry prefers to operate on
voluntary safety commitments,

34
00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.120
internal scaling policies, and polite
promises to do the right

35
00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.920
thing. Tech companies are offering ethical
guardrails they alone control.

36
00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.880
The Vatican is demanding actual legal
submission to external authorities.

37
00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:16.000
The geopolitical timing explains the
alliance.

38
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.760
In early 2026, Anthropic was locked in a
public dispute

39
00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:20.400
with the U.S.

40
00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.400
executive branch over whether government
agencies could use its models.

41
00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.960
They were under intense secular pressure.

42
00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.160
When a modern corporation faces a crisis
of trust, it

43
00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.560
often executes a legitimation move.

44
00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.680
You borrow the more authority of a highly
respected ancient

45
00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.480
institution to shield your own operations.

46
00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:41.920
Anthropic had spent months building this
specific bridge.

47
00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:45.040
Bishop Paul Ty had previously engaged with
the creation of

48
00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.440
Claude's constitutional AI, and Catholic
ethicists had filed amicus briefs

49
00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.800
defending Anthropic in federal disputes.

50
00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:54.760
Earning the only industry speaking slot at
a papal launch

51
00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.800
event tells regulators you are the
responsible adult in the

52
00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:01.400
room. It provides immense leverage against
domestic critics.

53
00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.240
The Vatican appearance was a highly
calculated exchange.

54
00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:09.400
Anthropic received political cover, and
the church secured a global

55
00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.400
spotlight for its encyclical.

56
00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.920
In public relations, there is a tactic
known as attentional

57
00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:19.560
displacement. You answer a difficult
question by loudly prioritizing a

58
00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.480
different, more favorable one.

59
00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:25.240
By using the Vatican stage to foreground
questions about model

60
00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:29.960
welfare, asking whether the AI has
internal states, Anthropic competes

61
00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:33.800
for the exact oxygen the encyclical needs
to highlight real-world

62
00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.520
third-party harms to human beings.

63
00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:38.920
This creates an epistemic trap.

64
00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.960
If the central debate of AI regulation
focuses on the

65
00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:45.520
inner suffering of the models, then only
the AI developers

66
00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:49.280
themselves have the technical access to
interpret that black box.

67
00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.840
Framing AI as a suffering entity naturally
keeps all diagnostic

68
00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.720
and regulatory power securely in the hands
of the tech

69
00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:01.440
companies. Conversely, if the debate
focuses on labor displacement, data

70
00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.840
theft, or autonomous weapons, the
investigative power shifts outward.

71
00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.320
It demands independent regulators.

72
00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:11.840
Asking society to worry about a model's
feelings forces us

73
00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:15.360
to blindly trust the developer's internal
judgment at the exact

74
00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:17.920
moment we need oversight from the outside.

75
00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.240
The Vatican anticipated this maneuver.

76
00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.880
Paragraph 107 of Magnifica Humanitas
delivers a blunt warning against

77
00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:28.000
relying on the tech industry's concept of
alignment.

78
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.880
It states that if we are satisfied with
merely aligning

79
00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:34.880
AI to human values without shared
standards of social justice,

80
00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:37.840
those who control AI will impose their own
moral vision

81
00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.240
as the, quote, invisible infrastructure of
society.

82
00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.240
Compute advantage is temporary.

83
00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.080
Tech monopolies rise and fall.

84
00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.840
Institutions are durable.

85
00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.400
The Vatican isn't asking for an aligned
model.

86
00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.120
It is asking for a binding, enduring
structure.

